@node Security policy
@chapter Security policy
@cindex security policy

The stance is the same as Gumdrop and Hopf: implement the modern,
defensible subset and nothing else.  Every item below is absent by
design, not disabled by default.  The lists are stated as code in
@file{include/gnuquic/policy.h}, and @file{tests/test-policy.c} asserts
that everything excluded here is rejected.

@menu
* Versions::
* Cipher suites::
* TLS 1.2 hardening::
